  "body": "Found during #3362.\n\n## What exists\n\n#3362 gives \"Pass starts at\" (Auto / Inside / Outside) to 3D Finish. Only Contour and Flat read it. The Geodesic pattern shows the line \"Not used with Geodesic\" under the row.\n\n## Why Geodesic is open\n\nGeodesic cuts rings of equal surface distance from the open edge of the model (`crates/motion/src/finishing3d/geodesic.rs`, the distance buckets and the `'levels` loop). The rings go outward from the open edge. Thus a start side exists in code. But the map from Inside and Outside to that start side is not clear:\n\n- Is \"Outside\" the open edge (today's start) and \"Inside\" the far ring?\n- Or does the start side follow the nesting of the rings in XY?\n\n## What to do\n\n- Decide the map, and record it in `docs/decisions/`.\n- If a map is decided: make `finishing3d::reads_pass_start` true for Geodesic, and reverse or reorder the distance levels for the forced value. Auto must keep today's moves byte for byte.\n- If no map is decided: keep the \"Not used\" line and record why.\n\n## Safety\n\nThe change can change posted moves. It is under the safety floor.\n\nRefs #3362\nRefs #3316\n",
